- POST /links with a destination longer than 2048 characters returns 400 and writes no row.
- POST /links with a malformed URL (no host, spaces, missing scheme) returns 400 and writes no row.
- POST /links without any authentication header succeeds (creation is open) provided the destination is valid.
- When the same client IP exceeds the configured creation rate limit within the window, POST /links returns 429 with a Retry-After header and writes no row; requests below the limit still return 201.
